<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/v3.1.1/saref.ttl> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://saref.etsi.org/saref4ener/v1.2.1/saref4ener.ttl> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-03-24"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The CELINE Core Ontology is a lightweight orchestration profile for\n    Renewable Energy Communities (RECs) and Digital Twin workflows. It connects established\n    standards — PECO, SAREF, SAREF4ENER, SOSA/SSN — without redefining their domain\n    semantics, providing a minimal coordination layer for simulation scenarios, dataset\n    references, KPI definition and evaluation, and REC flexibility commitment and settlement." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-09-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CELINE Core Ontology" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "celine" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/celine-eu#" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Version 0.6 adds registry-aligned grid topology (Substation,\n    PrimarySubstation, SecondarySubstation, PowerTransformer, DistributionFeeder),\n    regulatory zones, the GridOperator actor, a generalised ConnectionPoint superclass\n    for PECO Electric_POD, a presence-only asset inventory (PVSystem, BatteryStorage,\n    ElectricityMeter, EVCharger, HeatPump), member modeling (hasMember linkage, MemberRole\n    and MemberStatus vocabularies, hasDeliveryPoint for member-to-POD linkage), and\n    SharingGroup — a community partition for shared self-consumption accounting within a\n    regulatory zone, aligned with the RED II (2018/2001) double-counting prohibition.\n    CIM alignment via skos:closeMatch to IEC 61968 profile; SAREF alignment via\n    skos:closeMatch only — no new owl:imports. Asset technical attributes are intentionally\n    omitted; specs live in an external catalogue, addressed by celine:hasLocalIdentifier.\n    Version 0.7 adds hasDataset (asset/connection-point → DatasetReference) as the\n    operational counterpart to the SimulationRun-scoped usesDataset/producesDataset;\n    clarifies DatasetReference self-description via DCAT/DCT terms; generalises\n    external-catalogue wording to remove implementation-specific naming.\n    Version 0.8 is a conformance fix, no new terms: the CommitmentMode,\n    FlexibilityDirection, CostType and ConstraintType schemes gain the\n    skos:hasTopConcept assertions their SHACL shapes require — the concepts already\n    declared skos:inScheme and skos:topConceptOf, so only the scheme-side statement\n    was missing. All four schemes are flat, so every member is a top concept. Their\n    labels, prefLabels, descriptions and comments also gain the @en tag the other\n    nine schemes already carry.\n    Version 0.9 is a conformance fix, no new terms: the cim: prefix bound to\n    https://ontology.tno.nl/IEC_CIM/ — where TNO hosts a copy of CIM, not where CIM\n    mints its terms — so every skos:closeMatch to CIM resolved to nothing. It now\n    binds the IEC CIM100 namespace, http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#. Those alignments are\n    checked against the CIM100 class documentation rather than dereferenced: IEC CIM\n    is a paid standard and its namespace IRIs answer HTTP 403, so this is the one\n    external vocabulary CELINE references on documentary rather than resolvable\n    authority. celine:GridOperator also moves from cim:Company, which exists in no\n    CIM version, to cim:Organisation — note cim:Operator is a control-room person,\n    not the company.\n    Version 0.10 adds the observable properties a REC energy dataset actually\n    reports — grid import and export, self-consumed, collectively shared and\n    virtual consumed energy, and the self-consumption ratio — as\n    sosa:ObservableProperty individuals carrying qudt:hasQuantityKind. They exist\n    because no standard names them: quantitykind:Energy does not distinguish\n    import from export, and SAREF's saref:Energy is deprecated as of v3.2.1.\n    They give sosa:observedProperty a target that resolves. The energy mapping\n    specs previously pointed it at https://w3id.org/celine/property/* IRIs, which\n    are in neither this namespace (note celine-eu, not celine) nor any other, and\n    which nothing declared; the three forecast specs still do, and the forecast\n    properties they need are not minted here. Where a quantity also has a\n    celine:KPICatalog concept the two are linked with rdfs:seeAlso: the KPI is a\n    period total or rate, the observable property is what one observation\n    measures over one interval.\n    Version 0.11 finishes what v0.10 left open — the forecast half. celine:Forecast\n    is a sosa:Observation subclass, not a peco:Forecast: SOSA defines an Observation\n    as the act of a Procedure to \"estimate or calculate\" a value, which a computed\n    forecast is, and defines a Procedure as a reusable \"algorithm or computational\n    method\", which is what a forecasting model is. So sosa:usedProcedure names the\n    model through celine:ForecastModel, and the six observable properties above serve\n    measurement and forecast alike rather than being doubled. peco:Forecast was the\n    alternative and is well formed, but its peco:Property_of_interest requires a value\n    and a unit node, making a forecast three nested levels deep — unbuildable from the\n    flat rows every mapping spec here reads. Prediction bounds, confidence and the\n    forecast's target time are CELINE datatype properties so the node stays flat;\n    celine:forecastTargetTime is a literal shortcut for sosa:phenomenonTime, whose\n    time:TemporalEntity range would have reintroduced the nesting, in the same spirit\n    as SOSA's own sosa:hasSimpleResult shortcut for sosa:hasResult. celine:SpecificPVYield\n    is added as the seventh observable property and is the one that carries no\n    qudt:hasQuantityKind, deliberately: kWh/kWp is energy over power, so Energy and\n    DimensionlessRatio are both false and Time, while dimensionally right, reads as a\n    duration. geo: is bound for WGS84 coordinates and, like time:, is referenced without\n    being imported — the import set stays at four." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CELINE Core Ontology" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://celine-eu.github.io/> .
