<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#targetFlexibility> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#targetFlexibility> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCommitment> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#targetFlexibility> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#targetFlexibility> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Committed flexibility amount in kWh. Positive value; direction is expressed by hasFlexibilityDirection." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#targetFlexibility> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#targetFlexibility> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "target flexibility" .
# 
# 
# 
# #################################################################
# #
# #    Classes
# #
# #################################################################
# 
# 
# http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
# 
# https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Electric_POD
<https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Electric_POD> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ConnectionPoint> .
# 
# https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#EnergyCommunity
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#BatteryStorage
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#BatteryStorage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#BatteryStorage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Energy_storage> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#BatteryStorage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A battery energy storage system. Technical attributes live in an external catalogue."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#BatteryStorage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#BatteryStorage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Battery Storage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#BatteryStorage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Device> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CommunityContext
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CommunityContext> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CommunityContext> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Operational context binding a PECO Energy Community\n    with assets, datasets, simulations and flexibility commitments. Member\n    participation in this context is enumerated via celine:hasMember; each\n    member is linked to the wrapped peco:Energy_community via\n    peco:is_member_of (PECO predicate, reused as-is)." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CommunityContext> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CommunityContext> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Community Context" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CommunityContext> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:ctx1 a celine:CommunityContext ;\n    celine:hasCommunity    ex:rec_valdarno ;\n    celine:hasMember       ex:member_001 , ex:member_002 ;\n    celine:usesAsset       ex:pv_panel_01 ;\n    celine:hasSimulation   ex:sim_baseline ;\n    celine:hasCommitment   ex:fc_001 ;\n    celine:hasSettlementRun ex:sr_2025_q3 ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ConnectionPoint
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ConnectionPoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ConnectionPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A generalised point where a consumer or prosumer connects to the distribution grid. Country-specific identifier schemes (POD, CUPS, PRM, etc.) are captured via celine:hasIdentifierScheme. PECO Electric_POD is declared as a subclass."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ConnectionPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ConnectionPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Connection Point"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ConnectionPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#UsagePoint> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CostItem
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CostItem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CostItem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named cost voice within a SettlementRun (e.g., administrative fee,\n    platform fee, outstanding debt). Enables transparent cost breakdown before redistribution\n    amounts are finalised." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CostItem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CostItem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cost Item" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#CostItem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:cost_admin a celine:CostItem ;\n    celine:hasCostType  celine:AdminCost ;\n    dct:description     \"Community administration fee Q3 2025\" ;\n    celine:costAmount   \"120.00\"^^xsd:decimal .\n\nex:cost_platform_fee a celine:CostItem ;\n    celine:hasCostType  celine:Fee ;\n    dct:description     \"CELINE platform usage fee Q3 2025\" ;\n    celine:costAmount   \"45.00\"^^xsd:decimal ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DatasetReference
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DatasetReference> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DatasetReference> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reference to an external dataset used as input or produced as output.\n    CELINE does not define dataset schemas. Instances SHOULD declare their type or\n    conformance target (via dct:conformsTo), format (via dct:format), and an access\n    location (via dcat:accessURL or dct:source), using DCAT / Dublin Core terms." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DatasetReference> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DatasetReference> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dataset Reference" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DatasetReference> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:ds_irradiance a celine:DatasetReference ;\n    dct:identifier  \"irradiance-2025-07\" ;\n    dct:conformsTo  <https://example.org/some-dataset-profile> ;\n    dct:format      \"application/json\" ;\n    dcat:accessURL  <https://data.example.org/weather/irradiance> ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DistributionFeeder
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DistributionFeeder> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DistributionFeeder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Asset> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DistributionFeeder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A feeder line distributing power from a substation to downstream connection points."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DistributionFeeder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DistributionFeeder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Distribution Feeder"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#DistributionFeeder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#Feeder> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#EVCharger
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#EVCharger> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#EVCharger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Asset> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#EVCharger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An electric vehicle charging station. Technical attributes live in an external catalogue."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#EVCharger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#EVCharger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EV Charger"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#EVCharger> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Device> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ElectricityMeter
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ElectricityMeter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ElectricityMeter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Asset> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ElectricityMeter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A metering device measuring energy flows at a connection point or asset."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ElectricityMeter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ElectricityMeter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Electricity Meter"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ElectricityMeter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Device> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCommitment
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCommitment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCommitment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A member's pledge to provide a specific amount of flexibility\n    on one or more of their PODs during a given time window. The commitment can be\n    automated (device-driven) or voluntary (manually activated by the member)." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCommitment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCommitment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Flexibility Commitment" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCommitment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:fc_001 a celine:FlexibilityCommitment ;\n    celine:committedBy              ex:member_rossi ;\n    celine:onPOD                    ex:pod_rossi_heatpump ;\n    celine:hasCommitmentMode        celine:Automated ;\n    celine:hasFlexibilityDirection  celine:FlexDown ;\n    celine:targetFlexibility        \"2.5\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:hasTimeInterval          ex:interval_2025_07_01 ;\n    celine:generatesCredit          ex:cr_001 ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityConstraint
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Operational constraint governing when and how flexibility declared in a\n    FlexibilityEnvelope may be activated. Encodes timing rules (minimum notice period, minimum\n    and maximum activation duration, recovery time between activations) and frequency limits." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Flexibility Constraint" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:constraint_hp a celine:FlexibilityConstraint ;\n    celine:hasConstraintType     celine:DurationConstraint ;\n    celine:minNotificationTime   \"PT15M\"^^xsd:duration ;\n    celine:minActivationDuration \"PT30M\"^^xsd:duration ;\n    celine:maxActivationDuration \"PT4H\"^^xsd:duration ;\n    celine:minRecoveryTime       \"PT1H\"^^xsd:duration ;\n    celine:maxActivationsPerDay  \"3\"^^xsd:integer ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCredit
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCredit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCredit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Credit awarded to a member for fulfilling (fully or partially)\n    a FlexibilityCommitment. Denominated in kWh and backed by metered SOSA observations.\n    Credits accumulate until reconciled in a SettlementRun." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCredit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCredit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Flexibility Credit" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityCredit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:cr_001 a celine:FlexibilityCredit ;\n    celine:earnedBy     ex:member_rossi ;\n    celine:creditFor    ex:fc_001 ;\n    celine:creditAmount \"2.1\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:evidencedBy  ex:obs_pod_rossi_20250701T10 ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityEnvelope
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityEnvelope> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityEnvelope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Declared capability of a Point of Delivery (POD) to provide flexibility\n    within a given availability window. Captures the physical bounds — maximum upward and downward\n    power and available energy — that constrain any FlexibilityCommitment drawn from it.\n    Aligned with saref4ener:PowerProfile for device-level scheduling semantics." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityEnvelope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityEnvelope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Flexibility Envelope" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityEnvelope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://saref.etsi.org/saref4ener/> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityEnvelope> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:env_hp a celine:FlexibilityEnvelope ;\n    celine:envelopeFor           ex:pod_rossi_heatpump ;\n    celine:maxFlexUp             \"2.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:maxFlexDown           \"3.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:availableEnergy       \"6.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:hasAvailabilityWindow ex:window_morning ;\n    celine:hasConstraint         ex:constraint_hp ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityRequest
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityRequest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A demand signal issued by a community operator or automated system\n    requesting members to activate flexibility within a given time window. Specifies the\n    desired direction (FlexDown/FlexUp) and target amount. One request may result in zero,\n    one, or many FlexibilityCommitments from different members."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Flexibility Request"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#FlexibilityRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:req_001 a celine:FlexibilityRequest ;\n    celine:requestedBy              ex:dso_enel ;\n    celine:hasFlexibilityDirection  celine:FlexDown ;\n    celine:requestedFlexibility     \"10.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:hasTimeInterval          ex:interval_2025_07_01_peak ;\n    celine:hasRequestStatus         celine:RequestFulfilled ;\n    celine:resultsInCommitment      ex:fc_001 , ex:fc_002 ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Forecast
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Forecast> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Forecast> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Forecast> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An estimate of an observable property at a time later than the one at which the estimate was made. Distinguished from a measurement by celine:forecastTargetTime standing after sosa:resultTime, and by its type. Uses the same celine: observable properties as a measurement does, so a consumer comparing forecast against actual compares like with like."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Forecast> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Forecast> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Forecast"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Forecast> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Previsione"@it .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Forecast> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Forecast> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Forecast> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Forecast"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastModel
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastModel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Procedure> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The algorithm or computational method that produced a forecast — a statistical model, a physical simulation, or a foundation model. Reached through sosa:usedProcedure, which SOSA already declares for exactly this. Reusable: one individual per model, referenced by every forecast it produced, which is what makes 'which model said this' answerable after the fact."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Forecast model"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Modello previsionale"@it .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastModel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Forecast model"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastRun
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastRun> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One execution of a celine:ForecastModel, producing the series of forecasts that share a horizon. Exists so a series is addressable as one thing without sosa:ObservationCollection, which lives in the SSN extension rather than the sosa.ttl this profile imports — reaching for it would mean a fifth owl:imports, which is a design decision and not an editing step. A run is referenced by IRI; describing it further is deferred."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Esecuzione previsionale"@it .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Forecast run"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#ForecastRun> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Forecast run"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#GridOperator
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#GridOperator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#GridOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Agent> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#GridOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An entity that operates grid infrastructure. Typically a Distribution System Operator (DSO). Role-based modelling is deferred; class-based typing is consistent with PECO style."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#GridOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#GridOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grid Operator"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#GridOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#Organisation> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#HeatPump
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#HeatPump> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#HeatPump> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Asset> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#HeatPump> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A heat pump for space heating, cooling, or hot water. Technical attributes live in an external catalogue."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#HeatPump> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#HeatPump> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Heat Pump"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#HeatPump> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/HeatPump> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIDefinition
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A definition of a KPI type, independent of any specific evaluation.\n    Captures the name, description, formula, unit, scope, calculation method and temporal\n    granularity of a KPI. Instances may simultaneously be skos:Concept members of the\n    celine:KPICatalog controlled vocabulary."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Definizione KPI"@it .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "KPI Definition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://saref.etsi.org/saref4city/KeyPerformanceIndicator> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:kpi_def_ssr a celine:KPIDefinition , skos:Concept ;\n    skos:inScheme           celine:KPICatalog ;\n    celine:hasKPIName       \"Self-Sufficiency Rate\" ;\n    celine:hasKPIDescription \"Ratio of locally consumed energy to total consumption.\"@en ;\n    celine:hasKPIScopeType           celine:ScopeCommunity ;\n    celine:hasKPICalculationMethod   celine:MethodRatio ;\n    celine:hasKPITemporalGranularity celine:GranularityPeriod ;\n    celine:hasKPIUnit                celine:Dimensionless ." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> <http://bigg-project.eu/bigg4kpi#BuildingKeyPerformanceIndicator> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIEvaluation
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Evaluation of a KPI for a specific scope entity and time interval.\n    References a KPIDefinition for the metric type, and carries the computed value,\n    the evaluation period, and optional provenance links to observations or upstream\n    KPI evaluations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "KPI Evaluation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Valutazione KPI"@it .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://bigg-project.eu/bigg4kpi#KPIAssessment> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://saref.etsi.org/saref4city/KeyPerformanceIndicatorAssessment> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#KPIEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:kpi_eval_ssr_q3 a celine:KPIEvaluation ;\n    celine:hasKPIDefinition        celine:SelfSufficiencyRate ;\n    celine:hasKPIValue             \"0.72\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:hasEvaluationTimeInterval ex:interval_q3_2025 ;\n    celine:hasEvaluatedScope       ex:ctx1 ;\n    celine:hasInputObservation     ex:obs_meter_001 ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PVSystem
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PVSystem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PVSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Asset> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PVSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A photovoltaic system. Technical attributes (rated power, panel type, etc.) live in an external catalogue, addressed by celine:hasLocalIdentifier."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PVSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PVSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "PV System"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PVSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Device> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PowerTransformer
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PowerTransformer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PowerTransformer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Asset> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PowerTransformer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A transformer within a substation that converts between voltage levels."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PowerTransformer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PowerTransformer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Power Transformer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PowerTransformer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#PowerTransformer> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PrimarySubstation
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PrimarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PrimarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Substation> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PrimarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "HV/MV substation at the boundary between the transmission and distribution networks (e.g. Italian cabina primaria)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PrimarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PrimarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Primary Substation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#PrimarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#Substation> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RedistributionResult
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RedistributionResult> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RedistributionResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The calculated redistribution outcome for a single member within a\n    SettlementRun. Records credit balance (kWh), gross monetary value before deductions,\n    the member's allocated share of community costs, and the final net amount." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RedistributionResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RedistributionResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Redistribution Result" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RedistributionResult> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:result_rossi a celine:RedistributionResult ;\n    celine:resultFor        ex:member_rossi ;\n    celine:creditBalance    \"2.1\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:grossAmount      \"0.252\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:costDeduction    \"0.048\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:netAmount        \"0.204\"^^xsd:decimal ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RegulatoryZone
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RegulatoryZone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RegulatoryZone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Administrative coverage area defined by energy regulation, e.g. the service zone of a primary substation under Italian Decreto 199/2021 (GSE perimeter)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RegulatoryZone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#RegulatoryZone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Regulatory Zone"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Scenario
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Scenario> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Scenario> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Definition of assumptions, temporal scope and configuration\n    for one or more simulations." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Scenario> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Scenario> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Scenario" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Scenario> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:sc_summer a celine:Scenario ;\n    rdfs:label              \"Summer 2025 baseline\" ;\n    dct:description         \"24-hour simulation with historical irradiance data.\" ;\n    celine:hasTimeInterval  ex:interval_2025_summer ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SecondarySubstation
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SecondarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SecondarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Substation> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SecondarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "MV/LV substation serving end-user connection points (e.g. Italian cabina secondaria)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SecondarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SecondarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Secondary Substation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SecondarySubstation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#Substation> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SettlementRun
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SettlementRun> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SettlementRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Execution of the redistribution calculation for a settlement period.\n    Aggregates FlexibilityCredits across all members, applies a linear conversion rate\n    (kWh -> monetary), deducts shared cost voices (CostItems), and produces one\n    RedistributionResult per member." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SettlementRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SettlementRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Settlement Run" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SettlementRun> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:sr_2025_q3 a celine:SettlementRun ;\n    celine:settlesContext           ex:ctx1 ;\n    celine:hasTimeInterval          ex:interval_q3_2025 ;\n    celine:conversionRate           \"0.12\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    celine:currency                 \"EUR\" ;\n    celine:hasCostItem              ex:cost_admin, ex:cost_platform_fee ;\n    celine:hasRedistributionResult  ex:result_rossi, ex:result_bianchi ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SharingGroup
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SharingGroup> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SharingGroup> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A subset of community members whose energy flows are accounted together\n    for shared self-consumption within a single regulatory zone. Maps to the Italian\n    'configurazione' under Decreto 199/2021, the French 'périmètre ACC', and analogous\n    groupings in other EU member states. A connection point MUST NOT belong to more than\n    one SharingGroup across all communities — the double-counting prohibition derives from\n    RED II (2018/2001, Art. 22) and the Electricity Market Directive (2019/944, Art. 16)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SharingGroup> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SharingGroup> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sharing Group"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SharingGroup> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:group_north a celine:SharingGroup ;\n    rdfs:label              \"Northern area\" ;\n    celine:partitionOf      ex:ctx1 ;\n    celine:inRegulatoryZone ex:zone_cp_nord ;\n    celine:hasTopologyNode  ex:ss_AC221E00020 ;\n    celine:hasMember        ex:member_001 , ex:member_002 ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Simulation
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Simulation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Simulation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Abstract simulation definition independent from execution." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Simulation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Simulation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Simulation" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Simulation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:sim1 a celine:Simulation ;\n    celine:hasScenario      ex:sc_summer ;\n    celine:hasSimulationRun ex:run_001 ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SimulationRun
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SimulationRun> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SimulationRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Concrete execution of a Simulation under a specific Scenario." .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SimulationRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SimulationRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Simulation Run" .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#SimulationRun> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ex:run_001 a celine:SimulationRun ;\n    celine:usesDataset      ex:ds_irradiance ;\n    celine:producesDataset  ex:ds_energy_forecast ;\n    celine:hasKPIEvaluation ex:kpi_self_sufficiency ." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Substation
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Substation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Substation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.org/peco/peco-core#Asset> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Substation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Abstract superclass for electrical substations in the distribution grid."@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Substation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/celine-eu> .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Substation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Substation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/celine-eu#Substation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#Substation> .
